<%# One stacked bar per swipe statement, split by the card's response scale.

    Locals:
      result — an aggregate_results entry for a tap_card (needs :counts, :card)

    Written for the Verto results page and the Common Question results page,
    which had grown two copies of the same three-segment bar. It is a loop over
    TapScales rather than a hand-written Yes/Unsure/No triple, so a five-point
    card reports on five and neither page has to know that.

    The Common Question page is the only caller since 2026-09-21: the Verto's
    result cards moved onto the dark surface and draw a row per response
    (surveys/_result_cards) rather than one stacked bar, so every answer on a
    card is read the same way whatever its type. This page is still a light
    surface, hence the black captions below.

    Each segment is painted in its own response's colour and captioned in
    whichever of black or white reads on it (BrandPalette.contrast_text), so a
    creator who restyles an answer restyles its bar too. The last segment takes
    flex:1 rather than a width, so rounding never leaves a hairline gap.
%>
<% responses = TapScales.for_card(result[:card]) %>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;">
  <% result[:counts].each do |label, tallies| %>
    <% next unless tallies.is_a?(Hash) %>
    <% counts = responses.map { |r| tallies[r["key"]].to_i } %>
    <% total  = [ counts.sum.to_f, 1.0 ].max %>
    <% pcts   = counts.map { |c| ((c / total) * 100).round } %>
    <div>
      <div style="font-family:'ABeeZee',sans-serif;font-size: var(--text-xs);color:rgba(0,0,0,0.45);margin-bottom:3px;"><%= label.truncate(55) %></div>
      <div style="display:flex;height:18px;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden;">
        <% responses.each_with_index do |response, i| %>
          <% color = response["color"].presence || "#8B85FF" %>
          <% last  = (i == responses.length - 1) %>
          <div style="background:<%= color %>;<%= last ? 'flex:1;' : "width:#{pcts[i]}%;" %>display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
            <% if pcts[i] > 15 %>
              <span style="font-family:'Alata',sans-serif;font-size: var(--text-2xs);color:<%= BrandPalette.contrast_text(color) %>;white-space:nowrap;"><%= pcts[i] %>% <%= response["label"] %></span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <%# The legend wraps: six responses will not sit on one line under a bar. %>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:2px;gap:4px 8px;">
        <% responses.each_with_index do |response, i| %>
          <span style="font-family:'Alata',sans-serif;font-size: var(--text-2xs);color:<%= response["color"].presence || "#8B85FF" %>;"><%= response["label"] %> · <%= counts[i] %></span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
